==Bandits==
===Pointy===
----
{{Enemy Infobox|Pointy}}
{{Intents|Pointy}}

Uses {{Int|Pointy|Pointy Special}} every turn.

{{Clear}}

===Romeo===
----
{{Enemy Infobox|Romeo}}
{{Intents|Romeo}}

Always starts with {{Int|Romeo|Mock}}, then alternates between {{Int|Romeo|Agonizing Slash}} and {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}.

On {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, starts with {{Int|Romeo|Mock}}, then repeats the pattern of {{Int|Romeo|Agonizing Slash}}, {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}, {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}.

{{Clear}}

===Bear===
----
{{Enemy Infobox|Bear}}
{{Intents|Bear}}

Always starts with {{Int|Bear|Bear Hug}}, then alternates between {{Int|Bear|Lunge}} and {{Int|Bear|Maul}}.

{{Clear}}

==Notes==
* Although the fight can be quite dangerous and offers a [[Relic]] reward, it does not count as an [[Elite]] combat for the sake of {{R|Preserved Insect}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Slaver's Collar}}.
* If the player has {{R|Red Mask}}, the [[Act 3]] Event {{E|Tomb of Lord Red Mask}} will have an option to gain 222 [[Gold]] for free.

==Trivia==
* {{M|Romeo}} appears in the Card art for {{C|Distraction}}.
* {{M|Bear}} appears in the Card art for {{C|Rampage}} and {{C|A Thousand Cuts}}.

